        },
        "caption": {
          "zh": "1888年 · 伦敦国家美术馆",
          "en": "1888 · The National Gallery, London"
        },
        "kicker": "ACT I",
        "title": {
          "zh": "第一幕 · 幕布后面",
          "en": "Behind the curtain"
        },
        "text": {
          "zh": "德加一生画了大量芭蕾舞者。比起舞台上的光彩，他更喜欢画幕后：等待、休息、整理舞鞋的那些时刻。",
          "en": "Degas painted ballet dancers throughout his life. More than the glamour on stage, he loved the moments behind it: waiting, resting, adjusting a shoe."
        }
      },
      {
        "image": "images/ballet-dancers.jpg",
        "alt": {
          "zh": "德加《芭蕾舞者》1888，粉彩，伦敦国家美术馆",
          "en": "Edgar Degas, Ballet Dancers, 1888, pastel, The National Gallery, London"
        },
        "caption": {
          "zh": "1888年 · 伦敦国家美术馆",
          "en": "1888 · The National Gallery, London"
        },
        "kicker": "ACT II",
        "title": {
          "zh": "第二幕 · 画室里的“快照”",
          "en": "A “snapshot” made in the studio"
        },
        "text": {
          "zh": "这幅画看起来像是在后台当场画下的快照，其实是在画室里，用之前画的多张单人舞者习作组合起来的。",
          "en": "It looks like a snapshot drawn on the spot, but it was made in his studio, combining earlier studies of individual dancers."
        }
      },
      {
        "image": "images/ballet-dancers.jpg",
        "alt": {
          "zh": "德加《芭蕾舞者》1888，粉彩，伦敦国家美术馆",
          "en": "Edgar Degas, Ballet Dancers, 1888, pastel, The National Gallery, London"
        },
        "caption": {
          "zh": "1888年 · 伦敦国家美术馆",
          "en": "1888 · The National Gallery, London"
        },
        "kicker": "ACT III",
        "title": {
          "zh": "第三幕 · 2025年来到伦敦",
          "en": "To London in 2025"
